-extends "channels/channel_claim_form.html"
-load i18n compress temba

-block pre-form
  This channel type uses the new <a href="https://developer.twitter.com/en/docs/accounts-and-users/subscribe-account-activity/overview">Twitter Activity API.</a>
  You will need to <a href="https://developer.twitter.com/en/apply-for-access">apply for access</a> and
  <a href="https://developer.twitter.com/en/docs/accounts-and-users/subscribe-account-activity/guides/getting-started-with-webhooks">create a
  Twitter application</a>. Make sure your Twitter application has "Read, Write and Direct Message" permissions.

  .mt-2
    -blocktrans trimmed with name=brand.name
      After connecting your account, incoming direct messages will be automatically read by {{ name }}. You can also
      send direct messages to known contacts using their X handle.

  .mt-2
    -blocktrans trimmed
      Note that X limits direct messages to 250 sent or received per day. To exceed this limit, contact X to increase
      your account's limits.

  .alert-warning
    -blocktrans trimmed
      To receive direct messages from new followers, update your X account to allow <b>receiving direct messages from
      anyone</b> in your <a href="https://x.com/settings/security">X Security Settings</a>.

    .mt-2
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Check the box (as seen below), then click "Save Changes".

    .mt-2
      <img src="{{STATIC_URL}}images/twitter_settings.png"/>
